---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import InfoPage from '@/components/InfoPage.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Editorial Policy | Date Night Ideas" description="Our standards for researching, writing, reviewing, sourcing, and updating date night ideas." canonicalPath="/editorial-policy">
  <InfoPage eyebrow="Editorial policy" title="Specific, useful, and independently written." intro="Our catalog is researched from the public web, then rebuilt around the decisions couples actually need to make.">
    <h2>Source discovery</h2><p>We use broad search and an allowlisted collection process. We respect robots directives, site access rules, rate limits, authentication, and paywalls. Successful source fetches receive a metadata-only research receipt; source prose is not stored in the project.</p>
    <h2>Original editorial value</h2><p>Published text must add execution detail, constraints, variations, safety context, and a point of view. Copying, stitching multiple passages, or close paraphrasing a single source is prohibited.</p>
    <h2>AI assistance</h2><p>AI may help organize notes, flag duplication, draft structured fields, or prepare an image brief. It cannot be the source of an Idea: every published record needs accessible web research, an independent constraint edit, a unique review ID, and automated checks against repeated template language.</p>
    <h2>Images</h2><p>Images are either generated for this project or sourced under a documented free license. We record the intended placement, prompt or source, alt text, and approval status.</p>
    <h2>Corrections and removal</h2><p>We correct inaccurate constraints and remove material when a credible rights, safety, or sourcing concern is raised. Send correction or rights requests to <a href="mailto:hello@date-night-ideas.com">hello@date-night-ideas.com</a>.</p>
  </InfoPage>
</BaseLayout>
